\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Sells $22 Mln To Support Sol  \b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2005\par 21:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Peru entered into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday, selling $22 million to help ease volatility, an official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.  \par \par \uc2 That marks the first time that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold U.S. dollars since September 2002, the official added.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sol ended Wednesday at a midrate of PEN3.3895 on a spread of PEN3.3890-PEN3.3900, weaker than Tuesday's close at PEN3.3600 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.3590-PEN3.3610.  \par \par \uc2 The selling of U.S. dollars is a switch for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has bought U.S. dollars steadily as the sol gained strength on booming exports.  \par \par \uc2 It stopped buying U.S. dollars in early September as demand by banks and institutional investors for the greenback increased.  \par \par \uc2 The sol depreciated by an average of 1.6% in September, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.  \par \par \uc2 The sol has weakened due to, among other factors, the decision by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to leave its key reference rate unchanged since late last year.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Fernando Zavala said Wednesday in a radio interview that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell U.S. dollars was aimed at calming temporary volatility.  \par \par \uc2 "There aren't any fundamental reasons for a depreciation of the exchange rate," Zavala said, pointing to the nation's strong trade position.  \par \par \uc2 "We have always said that it is temporary volatility," Zavala added.  \par \par \uc2 Banco BBV Continental said this week in a report that the weakening trend in the sol has been amplified by low liquidity in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 It added that the weakening of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is temporary and will eventually reflect solid economic fundamentals, including Peru's trade surplus and low inflation.  \par \par \uc2 WestLB Research said in a report Wednesday that Peru's economy could expand by 6.0% this year. It also forecasts a trade surplus of $4.1 billion this year and around $4.4 billion next year, assuming that commodity prices remain close to current levels.  \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 12-10-05 1924GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051012e1ac000vm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
