\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2  Sol Unchanged After Record  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Stocks Fall  \b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2005\par 22:05\par \uc2 OsterDowJones Commodity Wire\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2005, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  Standard Attribution Statement: News Provided by COMTEX.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA, Jul 07, 2005 (ODC via Comtex) --  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sol ended unchanged Thursday after the Central Reserve Bank of Peru entered the market to purchase a record $150 million.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed strong demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the Finance Ministry held an auction of 12-year treasury bonds to help repurchase Paris Club debt.  \par \par \uc2 The sol ended unchanged at PEN3.2505 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.2500-PEN3.2510 in heavy trading.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday brought the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's purchases of U.S. dollars so far this year to $2.358 billion, above the $2.340 billion it bought in all of 2004, an official said.  \par \par \uc2 The key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 3.05% Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The Lima stock exchange, meanwhile, closed lower Thursday as several-blue chip stocks gave up recent gains.  \par \par \uc2 The stock market's broad general index fell 11.13 points, or 0.27%, to 4050.29, while the selective blue-chip index lost 19.32 points, or 0.29%, to close at 6614.38.  \par \par \uc2 Beverage producer Union de Cervecerias Peruanas Backus & Johnston SAA (BACKUSI.VL) fell 0.7% to end at 1.40 soles. There has been speculation that the company's controlling shareholder may be the target of a takeover bid.  \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) lost 1.3% to end at $3.93 as copper prices eased.  \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 07-07-05 1636ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020050707e17700563\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
