\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2 's Sol Strengthens Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Stocks Gain  \b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2005\par 21:05\par \uc2 OsterDowJones Commodity Wire\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2005, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  Standard Attribution Statement: News Provided by COMTEX.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA, Jan 26, 2005 (ODC via COMTEX) --  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sol continued to gain strength Wednesday, despite ongoing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which bought $18 million. The sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.2605 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.2600-PEN3.2610. The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.2665 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.2650-PEN3.2660. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly to help ease the appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also placed PEN50 million in overnight repurchase agreements, or repos, at an average annual yield of 3.02%. The key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 2.94% on Tuesday. Meanwhile, Lima's stock indexes rose Wednesday as a number of smaller companies gained ground. The broad general index gained 37.10 points, or 0.95%, to end at 3,931.22. The selective blue chip index rose 59.59 points, or 0.92%, to end at 6,524.04. Miner Sociedad Minera El Brocal SAA (BROCALC1.VL) climbed 12.8% to close at PEN7.40. The company told securities regulatory agency Conasev in a letter Wednesday that it didn't have any news to report that would have affected the share price. Manufacturer Alicorp SAA (ALICORC1.VL) gained 2.9% to end at PEN1.80 as consumer shares remained a favorite of investors.  \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 Copyright 2004 Dow Jones. All rights reserved.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020050126e11q006nr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
