\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Sol Ends Weaker; Stock Market Falls   \b0\par\par\uc2 246 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2005\par 22:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's sol weakened slightly Thursday after the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy $5 million.   \par \par \uc2 The sol closed at PEN3.2750 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.2740-PEN3.2760. The sol closed the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.2745 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.2740-PEN3.2750.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed PEN40 million in three-year certificates of deposit at an average annual yield of 6.27%, PEN50 million in two-year CDs at an average annual yield of 5.21%, and PEN30 million in 18-month CDs at an average annual yield of 4.81%. It also placed PEN40 million in seven-day CDs at an average annual yield of 2.98%.   \par \par \uc2 The key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 2.94% on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Lima's stock indexes fell Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 The broad general index fell 16.97 points or 0.45% to end at 3,719.45. The selective blue chip index slipped 27.78 points or 0.45% to end at 6,176.58.   \par \par \uc2 Miner Volcan SAA (VOLCABC1) fell 1.6% to end at PEN1.21 on weaker zinc prices.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Southern Peru Copper Corp.(PCU) fell 0.3% to end at $43.51 as copper prices dipped.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rebecca Howard, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 01-06-05 1653ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020050106e11600030\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
