\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Peru's Sol Strengthens; Stock Market Jumps Higher  \b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2004\par 21:04\par \uc2 OsterDowJones Commodity Wire\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2004, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  Standard Attribution Statement: News Provided by COMTEX.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA, Dec 15, 2004 (ODC via COMTEX) --  \par \par \uc2 Peru's sol strengthened Wednesday as demand remained strong from employers seeking the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pay year-end bonuses to workers. The sol strengthened despite ongoing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which bought $39.5 million after purchasing $67.5 million Tuesday and $30 million Monday. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is free floating and the only thing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does is to avoid volatility," central reserve bank director Eduardo Iriarte said on CPN radio. The sol closed Wednesday at a midrate of PEN3.2670 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.2660-PEN3.2680. The sol closed the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.2705 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.2700-PEN3.2710. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also placed PEN40 million in 18-month certificates of deposit at an average annual yield of 5.21%. It also placed PEN60 million of one-year CDs at an average annual yield of 4.52%, and another PEN50 million of nine-month CDs at an average yield of 4.16%. The key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 2.90% on Tuesday. Meanwhile, Lima's stock indexes ended sharply higher Wednesday as metal prices gained. The broad general index rose 40.56 points, or 1.14%, to end at 3,583.98. The selective blue chip index increased 69.35 points, or 1.18%, to end at 5,935.45. Precious metals miner Buenaventura SAA (BVN) gained 0.3% to end at PEN74.25 on rising gold prices. Southern Peru Copper Corp. (PCU) increased 0.9% to end at $45.50 on stronger copper prices.  \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 Copyright 2004 Dow Jones. All rights reserved.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020041217e0cf0006d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
