\par\par \b \uc2 Peru Exporter Group Calls On Govt To Halt Sol Strength  \b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2004\par 17:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's exporters said the sol will likely continue to appreciate in the short run and called on the government to rein in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The Exporters' Association, or ADEX, said the sol will strengthen as companies pay a traditional year-end extra monthly salary. An upcoming tax payment period is also seen creating demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The weakening of the dollar is having a detrimental effect for our exporters," the president of ADEX's clothing industry sector, Pedro Gamio, said Tuesday in a telephone interview.  \par \par \uc2 The sol, which appreciated by 4.8% in November over the previous 12-month period, broke through the important PEN3.30-per-dollar barrier Friday, closing at a midrate of PEN3.2985. It closed Monday unchanged.  \par \par \uc2 The sol's strength comes despite recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease its appreciation. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased about $2.0 billion so far this year, boosting net international reserves to $12.34 billion.  \par \par \uc2 But economists say that the fact the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  abstained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday and Monday may signal a change in strategy.  \par \par \uc2 "This reveals that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to permit a greater appreciation of the sol," the economic studies department of BBVA Banco Continental said in a report late Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The sol has gained strength due to a number of factors, including a boom in mineral exports.  \par \par \uc2 Peru posted a trade surplus totaling $284 million in October, compared with $58 million in the same month last year. For the 12-month period to October, the trade surplus totaled $2.38 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Among other things, the nation's exporters want the government to increase the limits that private pension funds have on investing outside the country, saying this would create demand for dollars.  \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 07-12-04 1608GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020041207e0c70000m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
