\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Peru's Sol Weakens; Stock Market Ends Higher  \b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2004\par 21:04\par \uc2 OsterDowJones Commodity Wire\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2004, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  Standard Attribution Statement: News Provided by COMTEX.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA, Nov 10, 2004 (ODC via COMTEX) --  \par \par \uc2 Peru's sol weakened Wednesday after the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy $15 million. The sol closed the session at a midrate of PEN3.3095 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.3090-PEN3.3100. The sol closed the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.3070 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.3060-PEN3.3080. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed PEN40 million in one-year certificates of deposit at an average annual yield of 4.64%, another PEN60 million in seven-month CDs at an average annual yield of 4.16% and another PEN225 million in seven-day CDs at an average annual yield of 3.07%. The key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 2.95% on Tuesday. Meanwhile, Lima's stock indexes ended higher Wednesday as some key mining companies gained ground. The broad general index increased 7.28 points, or 0.20%, to end at 3590.39. The selective blue chip index gained 7.20 points, or 0.12%, to end at 5955.45. Peru's largest financial services holding company, Credicorp Ltd. (BAP) rose 3.8% to end at $14.80. Credicorp this week reported third-quarter consolidated net income of $32.9 million compared with $26.0 million in the same quarter of the previous year. Southern Peru Copper Corp. (PCU) increased 1.8% to end at $45.80 even as copper prices dropped. -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 Copyright 2004 Dow Jones. All rights reserved.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020041112e0ba001fp\par }\page {\