\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Market Hits New Record High: Sol Ends Flat  \b0\par\par\uc2 284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2004\par 23:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Lima's stock indexes continued to climb Tuesday as investors sought several blue chip shares.  \par \par \uc2 The broad general index rose 30.51 points, or 0.88%, to end at 3485.84, another record high.  \par \par \uc2 The selective blue chip index increased 37.54 points, or 0.65%, to end at 5807.05.  \par \par \uc2 Food manufacturer Alicorp SAA (ALICORC1.VL) continued to attract investor interest, rising a strong 15.8% to end at 1.10 soles. ($1=PEN3.3085)  \par \par \uc2 Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) rose 2.2% to end at $4.24 as investors continued to be encouraged by the news that majority-owner Phelps Dodge Corp. had approved an $850 million expansion to Cerro Verde to increase copper output.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Peru's sol strengthened early in the session but ended flat when the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy $30 million.  \par \par \uc2 The sol closed the session at a midrate of PEN3.3085 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.3080-PEN3.3090, unchanged from Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed four series of certificates of deposit: PEN80 million in 14-month CDs at an average annual yield of 4.84%; PEN65 million in 38-day CDs at an average annual yield of 3.18%; PEN100 million in one-week CDs at an average annual yield of 3.05%; and another PEN40 million in one-week CDs at an average annual yield of 3.08%.  \par \par \uc2 The key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 2.77% on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par -By Rebecca Howard, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.co