\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Sol Strengthens; Stocks Rise  \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2004\par 23:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's sol closed stronger Monday despite Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy $10 million.  \par \par \uc2 The sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.3765 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.3760-PEN3.3770.  \par \par \uc2 The sol had closed the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.3905 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.3900-PEN3.3910.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a report late Friday that during August the sol appreciated by a nominal 1.3%, and by 2.2% during the year to the end of that month.  \par \par \uc2 "This movement reflects the weak expectations of a depreciation of the sol as the external situation remains favorable, and in a continuing stable regional context," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  added.  \par \par \uc2 On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed PEN80 million in 10-month certificates of deposit at an average annual yield of 4.34%, and another 40 million in six-month CDs at an average annual yield of 3.85%.  \par \par \uc2 The key average overnight lending rate in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 2.75% on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Lima's stock indexes ended higher Monday as some smaller shares gained ground.  \par \par \uc2 The general index rose 0.23%, or 6.48 points, to end at 2855.73.  \par \par \uc2 The selective blue chip index increased 0.11%, or 5.09 points, to end at 4707.14.  \par \par \uc2 Peruvian beverage producer Union de Cervecerias Peruanas Backus & Johnston SAA, or Backus, rose 1.0% to end at PEN1.03, while Peru's largest cement maker Cementos Limos also gained 1.0% to end at PEN3.20, the Lima Stock Exchange said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 09-06-04 1721ET ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1071 1837  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020040906e0960001z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
